# BUILD-MOD-6L pass 10: a world cooked without LandscapeCore reports every tile record as an Issue - WorldCook and
# WorldGen take `--disable-module LandscapeCore` (Tools/Shared/ToolModules.hpp; UE -DisablePlugins=). The DesertCtl
# lines below are rerun unchanged; [unregistered_issue] at the end is the pass 10 proof.
# BUILD-MOD-6L pass 9: the World Partition rules name no landscape key. Core/Serialize/WorldPartitionRules lists no
# landscape loading row, entity reference or component name; LandscapeCore::StartupModule registers them, its HLOD
# builder components and its activation kind (UE: the Landscape module owns FLandscapeActorDesc). A record whose
# component no started module registers is an Issue and is placed nowhere (WorldPartitionPlan::UnregisteredRecords).
# The pass 8 lines below are rerun unchanged.
# BUILD-MOD-6L pass 8: Core stops knowing the landscape. World Partition's rules (Core/Serialize/WorldPartitionRules)
# place a landscape tile and spline through a descriptor hook LandscapeCore registers (UE: FLandscapeActorDesc, the
# Landscape module's FWorldPartitionActorDesc subclass); LandscapeCore sits ABOVE Core and the dedicated server names it.
# The pass 6 lines below are rerun unchanged: WP_Protocol streams as on dev, G3_TwoTerrains draws its two landscapes.
# [server_bc01] also: `grep -n Landscape` over Desert/Desert/Source/Engine/Core finds no #include of LandscapeCore in a
# file of the module Core.
# BUILD-MOD-6L pass 6: the last Engine/World/Landscape files left Core - the runtime data (Data, Layout, TileFiles,
# Frame, LayerLimits, CollisionShape, Splines, SplinesJson, EditLayers, EditLayerStack) into the render-free module
# LandscapeCore (Desert/Landscape/Source/LandscapeCore), the edit tools (Brush, Paint, EditCache) into Landscape.
# WP_Protocol must stream as on dev; G3_TwoTerrains (two sculpted landscapes, Ground layer, tile height files) must draw
# exactly as the same scene on the dev Editor (frames/dev, shot before the move); saved as a new scene (tile height files
# written beside it by the module's save hook) and reopened, it draws the same (no lost layers or tiles).
# The dedicated server reaches the tiles through LandscapeCore: runner <scratch>/BUILD-MOD-6L/run_server7.sh (Release DesertServer
# --role all on the cooked WP_Protocol + one DesertNetProbe bot spawned 20 m over the terrain).
Проект Projects/Desert/Desert.deproj --scene Content/Scenes/WP_Protocol.desce
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Тогда 0_wp_protocol WP_Protocol как в dev: ландшафт, город, небо; стриминг (8 из 602 сущностей, как в dev); без падения и диалога ошибки
Когда run Scene "Open Scene G3_TwoTerrains.desce"
Когда wait-idle 60
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Position -10000,9000,12000
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0,-0.5,-0.866
Когда frames 60
Тогда-вид 1_landscape оба ландшафта G3_TwoTerrains с рельефом и слоем Ground, как в кадре dev той же сцены; в editor.log нет "missing module" и "unregistered component"
Когда save-as G3_TwoTerrains_6L
Когда run Scene "Open Scene G3_TwoTerrains_6L.desce"
Когда wait-idle 60
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Position -10000,9000,12000
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0,-0.5,-0.866
Когда frames 60
Тогда-вид 2_saved_reopened G3_TwoTerrains, сохранённая как G3_TwoTerrains_6L и открытая заново: оба ландшафта с тем же рельефом и слоем Ground, что в 1_landscape (тайлы и слои не потеряны); в editor.log нет ошибки сохранения ландшафта и отказа тайла
# [B-C01] server_collision (run_server7.sh, not a DesertCtl step): server.log residency-union lines carry
# "collision N body(ies) (N landscape tile(s))" with N > 0 and no "[Server] landscape" error; the bot's pawn,
# spawned 20 m over the terrain at (2500, 2000, 650), lands and then stands at one height (no fall through).
# [unregistered_issue] pass 10 (WorldCook, not a DesertCtl step; G3_TwoTerrains is not a partitioned world - WorldCook
# refuses it, "lists no ExternalEntities" - so the tiled world is WP_Protocol, 16 landscape tiles): from Projects/Desert,
#   WorldCook Content/Scenes/WP_Protocol.desce --out <scratch>/wc10/on --project Desert.deproj --project-registry
#   WorldCook Content/Scenes/WP_Protocol.desce --out <scratch>/wc10/off --project Desert.deproj --project-registry \
#             --disable-module LandscapeCore
# Without the module (no code edited, no other build) stdout says "module LandscapeCore not started" and carries one
# Issue per landscape tile record naming its component ("'LandscapeTile', which no module started in this process
# registers"), the StreamingGeneration log's summary "N record(s) of a component no started module registers" and no
# "composite of Landscape Tile" footprint; with it the cook prints 0 World Partition issue(s) and the log places the
# 16 tiles as on dev.
